===== verdict
"HARNESS-ROUTE-DEFECT"
===== notAClaim
[
 "Plane crossings are NOT a certification of the passage. Crossing every original incoming plane while supported proves geometry and support only; the contract's credited quantity is routeProgressUnits, which the crossings do not exercise.",
 "No acceptance, no creative redesign, no eighth repair proposed."
]
===== observedFacts
[
 {
  "atMs": 70877,
  "fact": "vertex-2 plane crossed at pose z=16.164333 (0.164 PAST the vertex on the incoming +z axis); credit 4.008321486093145; supported true"
 },
 {
  "atMs": 71644,
  "fact": "vertex-3 crossed at [-44.028859,50.989046,16.164333]; credit steps to exactly 6 and never changes again"
 },
 {
  "atMs": "72145..74948",
  "fact": "vertices 4..9 all crossed, supported true every sample, credit constant 6 over ~12 further walked units"
 },
 {
  "atMs": 74950,
  "fact": "gate all-original-incoming-planes-crossed-in-order ok:true while gate terra-full-eighteen-unit-ordered-passage failed on fullEighteenCredited only"
 },
 {
  "source": "commonGroundDirector.ts:1320",
  "fact": "credit call is routeProgressUnits(CG_ROUTE_COMMON, body, common.terraUnits, displacement), gated on walkedSegmentSupported && checkReference; both were live-true here (supported:true, referenceHeldDuringPassage:true)"
 },
 {
  "source": "commonGroundRoute.ts:467-503",
  "fact": "ceiling = previousUnits + displacementUnits, recomputed per frame from CREDIT (not from the body's true arc); an arc claim above the ceiling is refused outright, and the doc block at :437-465 states this frontier lock is deliberate"
 },
 {
  "source": "commonGroundState.ts:113",
  "fact": "CG_ROUTE_COMMON vertices are 2 units apart, so arc at vertex i is exactly 2i; credit 6 == vertex 3 exactly"
 }
]
===== missingCondition
{
 "statement": "Re-traversal after a deviation must resume with the body's route projection at or behind the credited frontier ON EVERY segment, including the OUTGOING leg's axis at each corner. A residual displacement past a corner vertex along that corner's incoming axis is lateral (uncredited) on the next leg, but becomes LONGITUDINAL again at the next corner that turns back onto that axis, where the projected arc jumps discontinuously by that residual. Credit can absorb a jump only if it is <= one frame's displacement.",
 "quantities": {
  "residualCarriedFromVertex2Units": 0.164333,
  "perFrameDisplacementCeilingUnits": 0.0836,
  "note": "0.0836 = measured unitsPerMs 0.005014681287175485 * 1000 / 60 Hz",
  "consequence": "0.1643 > 0.0836, so the arc discontinuity at vertex 3 (6 -> 6.164) is refused; thereafter the gap only grows and the lock is permanent, exactly as commonGroundRoute.ts:446-451 documents"
 },
 "harnessCause": {
  "file": "verifier/probes/arrival-common-manual/common-passage-probe.mjs:590-592",
  "code": "aim = [vertex[0] + plane.normal[0]*0.15, vertex[1], vertex[2] + plane.normal[1]*0.15]; toPlane = max(0,-offset) + 0.15",
  "why": "The plane step deliberately aims 0.15 PAST each vertex along that vertex's incoming normal, and the 30 ms minimum pulse quantises to ~0.15 units (0.1204 commanded + 0.0274 coast). At a corner the incoming normal is the axis the route later re-uses, so every corner step manufactures a 0.06-0.17 unit residual on a later leg's longitudinal axis - roughly twice the per-frame credit ceiling."
 }
}
===== instrumentationLimitation
{
 "helper": "verifier/probes/arrival-common-manual/commonPassageLogic.mjs:186 orderedFrontierVerdict",
 "defect": "It checks only ordered indices, non-decreasing atMs, crossed===true, finite units, and MONOTONIC units (b.units + eps >= a.units). A constant credit of 6 across vertices 3..9 satisfies every one of those. It never asserts units >= 2*index (the route's own arc at vertex index), so the gate all-original-incoming-planes-crossed-in-order reported ok:true on the exact run whose credit was frozen.",
 "effect": "The ordered-frontier gate is not evidence of credited progress and must not be read as partial certification."
}
===== nextMeasurement
{
 "smallestFalsifiable": "Re-run the SAME deviation-1 script with one bounded harness change: at each plane step aim to the vertex MINUS 0.05 along the incoming normal and require the outgoing-leg axis residual |offset| <= 0.05 before turning; assert live credit >= 2*vertexIndex - 0.05 at every crossing. Prediction from the replay: credit follows 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 16, 18 and the passage gate passes with no game change.",
 "falsifies": "If credit still freezes at 6 with a verified sub-0.05 residual at every corner while supported and reference-held stay true, the harness explanation is dead and a live game-side cause must be sought."
}
